id: afterimage-technique
name: Afterimage Technique
# "Ability Type: Technical/Magical" - chosen when it is gained.
uaType: both
prerequisite: Agility Score 4+
tpCost: 8
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 2
# "When targeted by an Attacking Maneuver, you can increase your Defense Value by 2(T) for the duration of
# the Attacking Maneuver. If you avoid the Attacking Maneuver, you can use the Movement Maneuver as an
# Out-of-Sequence Action. This Movement Maneuver does not trigger the Exploit Maneuver."
evadeDefense: 2
evadeOffer: movement
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Counter Maneuver when attacked: Defense Value 2(T) higher for that attack, and if it misses, a Movement
  out of sequence that provokes no Exploit. Passive: Rapid Movement's Strike bonus 1(T) higher.
text: >
  Afterimage Technique: You possess the ability to move faster than the naked eye can see, allowing you to
  create visual illusions of your presence in locations that you are no longer in or to seemingly vanish
  when attacked.
  –Ability Type: Technical/Magical
  –Prerequisites: Agility Score 4+
  –TP Cost: 8
  –KP Cost: 2(T)
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 1 Counter Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: Increase the bonus to your Strike Roll from Rapid Movement by 1(T).
  –Effect: When targeted by an Attacking Maneuver, you can increase your Defense Value by 2(T) for the
  duration of the Attacking Maneuver. If you avoid the Attacking Maneuver, you can use the Movement
  Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Action. This Movement Maneuver does not trigger the Exploit Maneuver.

---

# Offered in Respond to whoever it targets, among their Counter Maneuvers: 2(T) KP and a Counter Action,
# once per Combat Round, and the Dodge that answers the attack carries the 2(T) as a row of its own. Avoided,
# the card offers the Movement out of sequence, and that Movement offers no Exploit.

# "Increase the bonus to your Strike Roll from Rapid Movement by 1(T)." Rapid Movement's bonus is held as
# the `rapid` Resource until the end of the turn (maneuvers/movement.dbu); while it is, 1(T) more.
[passive]
if (rapid.stacks > 0) {
  strike += 1(T);
}
